      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKZINO (7) ran an encouraging race on debut here over 1300m, in the market and working home well for a narrow third. She's bred to run a trip so the rise to 1600m now looks ideal for the Begg stable and she draws for every hope in what looks a very winnable affair given she handled a soft 6 on debut. ONLY OPERA (6) ran a solid race fresh at Geelong when third on similarly heavy ground, beaten four lengths. Fitter for that and up in trip should suit. KOYUGA RIP (1) has run fourth in all four runs this campaign, he's rock hard fit and will likely lead, consider on that alone. AZULITA (3) is going okay and in the mix with heavy track experience.",
